{
 "kind": "job_benchmark",
 "date": "2026-10-06",
 "scope": "Whole Quick Sim jobs of the 27 single-target production requests (fixtures/mage/prepared-v2/production-*.request.json) at 3000 iterations, the production Quick Sim size, run as the worker would from a bundle after the exporter reads a tank's swing from the stat aura simulations and route.py gates in the Rust simulation process: Go as one pinned engine process on the request, Rust as tools/route.py with the Go exporter's prepare and one Rust process that gates the prepared input and simulates it.",
 "method": "tools/job_bench.py interleaves the Go job, the routed Rust job and route.py's two steps on their own, three rounds per request; each figure is the median over the rounds. Wall time is measured around each process; CPU time and peak resident set come from wait4 and include every process a job waits for. Overhead is a job's wall time minus the engine's own iteration loop time. The throughput phase runs every request's job three times, four jobs at a time, in each engine. The record it follows, 2026-10-06-whole-jobs.json, ran the gate as a separate check process, so its steps are prepare, check and sim; here the gate is part of sim.",
 "command": "python3 tools/job_bench.py --bundle <scratch>/bundle-69d29a29e --output <scratch>/report.json --rounds 3 --iterations 3000 --concurrency 4",
 "source_revision": "69d29a29e03aaabe751e840627074c12f5f6752a",
